**TASK III (10 marks)**

The C and Pascal programs below are implementations of an algorithm that puts in place a validation rule to ensure that a valid score between 0 and 20 inclusive is input by the user.

**C Program**

```c
#include <stdio.h>
int main(void) {
    float score;
    printf("Enter your test score please (between 0 and 20): ");
    scanf("%f", &score);
    while ((score < 0) || (score > 20)) {
        printf("Enter a valid score\n");
        printf("Enter your test score please (between 0 and 20): ");
        scanf("%f", &score);
    }
    printf("Validated score entered\n");
    getchar();
}
```

**Pascal Program**

```pascal
Program ScoreValidation;
Var
  score : real;
Begin
  write('Enter your test score please (between 0 and 20): ');
  readln(score);
  while ((score < 0 ) or (score > 20 )) do
  begin
    writeln('Enter a valid score');
    write('Enter your test score please (between 0 and 20): ');
    readln(score);
  end;
  writeln('Validated score entered');
  readln;
End.
```
